WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.577
The first project step is inspection.

00:00:02.577 --> 00:00:06.567
In Spark, printSchema helps you see column types.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:11.032
show displays sample records. count can be useful, but remember that it triggers work.

00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:13.167
Use it intentionally.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:20.757
Before writing transformations, know what the raw data looks like and what one row represents.

00:00:20.757 --> 00:00:26.102
Connect this idea to a lakehouse processing millions of web events across many files.

00:00:26.102 --> 00:00:31.067
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:37.892
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:43.112
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:48.320
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
